==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hvítr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hwītaz}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱweytos}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈxʷiːtʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːtʏr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj-01|hvít|hvítt|hvítari|hvítastur}}

# [[white]]
#: ''Hún var '''hvít''' sem snjór.''
#:: She was '''white''' as snow.

====Inflection====
{{is-decl-adj-1|hv|í|t}}

====Derived terms====
* [[hrímhvítur]]
* [[hvítur fyrir hærunum]] (with greying hair)
* [[hvítblæði]] (leukaemia)
* [[hvítasunna]] (Whitsun, Whitsuntide)
* [[hvítkál]] (white cabbage) {{taxlink|Brassica oleracea var. capitata f. alba|form}}
* [[hvítlaukur]] (garlic)
* [[hvítna]] (to turn white, to pale)
* [[hvítrússneska]] (Byelorussian)
* [[Hvítarússland]] (White Russia)
* [[hvítstorkur]] (a white stork)
* [[hvítvín]]
* [[hvítabjörn]]
* [[svart á hvítu]] (black and white)
* [[sjá svart á hvítu|sjá eitthvað svart á hvítu]] (to see something in black and white)

====Related terms====
* [[hvíta]] (white of an egg)

====See also====
* [[hæra]]

